Slide 9 — Problem 1: Monetization + ROI
Pricing: SaaS fee per active project / sales seat, scaled by lead volume (e.g., $200–500/mo/project) + outcome kicker tied to conversion uplift
Sample math: project gets 1,000 leads/month at ₹1,000/lead spend = ₹10L/month ad spend. If response-time improvement lifts site-visit conversion from 3% → 5%, that's ~20 extra site visits/month for the same spend — a direct, quantifiable cost-per-sale reduction
Pitch: "we reduce the leakage between what you already spend on leads and what you convert"
Slide 10 — Problem 2: Post-sale ops & collections
After booking, buyer enters an 18–36 month relationship: payments, status queries, handover, defects
Currently handled by a thin CRM/accounts team via calls and email
Directly affects cash flow (collections/DSO) and buyer satisfaction (referrals, repeat business)
Natural bookend to Problem 1 — same buyer/unit data model, covers the full lifecycle
