Slide 12 — Problem 2: Monetization + ROI
Pricing: per-unit-under-management fee (e.g., $5–15/unit/month through possession + defect-liability period), or a small % fee on overdue amounts actually collected
Sample math: a 400-unit project with 10% of installments running late each cycle — faster reminders + one-tap payment links recovering even half of that late-pay gap shortens DSO meaningfully, which is a direct, financeable cash-flow improvement
Pitch: "we get you paid faster and cut your support ticket load, for a fee smaller than one collections hire"
Slide 13 — Why these two together
Bookend the full customer lifecycle: acquisition (Problem 1) → retention/ops (Problem 2)
Share one buyer/unit data model — natural two-product platform, not disconnected point solutions
Both are text/voice/document workflows — buildable now with current agentic LLM + tool-use patterns, no vision/robotics dependency
Both tie to a number the developer already tracks — easy "before vs after" ROI pitch
